## What Problem This Solves

Fixes https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/105683

Config files with JSON5 comments (`// inline` or `/* block */`) get comments silently stripped when `openclaw config set` writes back. This causes data loss for users who rely on comments for documentation.

## User Impact

- Users see a warning before their JSON5 comments are stripped on config write
- No breaking changes: the behavior is unchanged, just a warning is added

## Evidence

### Proof 1: `//` line comment detection (real terminal output)

```
$ node --import tsx -e '
const { checkCommentLossWarning } = await import("./src/config/json5-comments.ts");

const config = "{\n  // gateway channel mode\n  \"agents\": {\n    \"defaults\": {\n      \"model\": \"claude-sonnet-4-6\"\n    }\n  }\n}";

console.log("=== BEFORE: config write would silently strip comments ===");
console.log(config);

console.log("\n=== AFTER: checkCommentLossWarning detects and warns ===");
const warned = [];
checkCommentLossWarning(config, "/home/user/.openclaw/openclaw.json5", (msg) => warned.push(msg));
console.log("WARNING:", warned[0]);
'

=== BEFORE: config write would silently strip comments ===
{
  // gateway channel mode
  "agents": {
    "defaults": {
      "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6"
    }
  }
}

=== AFTER: checkCommentLossWarning detects and warns ===
WARNING: Config write will strip JSON5 comments from /home/user/.openclaw/openclaw.json5. Use a separate tool to re-add documentation comments after modifications.
```

### Proof 2: `/* */` block comment detection (real terminal output)

```
$ node --import tsx -e '
const { checkCommentLossWarning } = await import("./src/config/json5-comments.ts");

const config = "{/* agent defaults */\"agents\":{\"defaults\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-4-6\"}}}";

const warned = [];
checkCommentLossWarning(config, "/home/user/.openclaw/openclaw.json5", (msg) => warned.push(msg));
console.log("WARNING:", warned[0]);
'

WARNING: Config write will strip JSON5 comments from /home/user/.openclaw/openclaw.json5. Use a separate tool to re-add documentation comments after modifications.
```

### Proof 3: No false positives — URL `//` and normal JSON do not trigger

```
$ node --import tsx -e '
const { checkCommentLossWarning } = await import("./src/config/json5-comments.ts");

// URL containing // should not trigger
const urlConfig = "{\"apiUrl\":\"https://api.example.com/v1\"}";
const r1 = checkCommentLossWarning(urlConfig, "/tmp/test.json5", () => {});
console.log("URL // result:", r1 === undefined ? "undefined (no false positive) ✓" : "FALSE POSITIVE ✗");

// Normal JSON with no comments should not trigger
const normalConfig = "{\"agents\":{\"defaults\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-4-6\"}}}";
const r2 = checkCommentLossWarning(normalConfig, "/tmp/test.json5", () => {});
console.log("Normal JSON result:", r2 === undefined ? "undefined (no false positive) ✓" : "FALSE POSITIVE ✗");

// skipOutputLogs suppresses warning
const r3 = checkCommentLossWarning("{\n  // comment\n  \"key\": \"val\"\n}", "/tmp/test.json5", () => {}, true);
console.log("skipOutputLogs result:", r3 === undefined ? "undefined (suppressed) ✓" : "NOT SUPPRESSED ✗");
'

URL // result: undefined (no false positive) ✓
Normal JSON result: undefined (no false positive) ✓
skipOutputLogs result: undefined (suppressed) ✓
```

### Before/After Summary

| Scenario | BEFORE (without fix) | AFTER (with fix) |
|---|---|---|
| Config has `//` comments | comments silently stripped | WARNING emitted |
| Config has `/* */` comments | comments silently stripped | WARNING emitted |
| Normal JSON, no comments | no action | no warning (correct) |
| URL contains `://` | no action | no warning (correct, no false positive) |
| `skipOutputLogs=true` | N/A | warning suppressed (correct) |

## Tests

### Test coverage

```
$ node scripts/test-projects.mjs src/config/io.write-config.test.ts src/config/mutate.test.ts
Tests  130 passed (135)
  5 failed — all pre-existing SQLite failures on Node 25.1.0, unrelated to this change
```

### Test files added

- `src/config/json5-comments.test.ts` — 9 tests: warn, no-warn, false-positives, string-embedded comments, escaped quotes, skipOutputLogs, logger.warn channel, rejected writes, backtracking proof
- `src/config/mutate.test.ts` — 3 tests: warns for $include file with comments, no warn for clean $include, skipOutputLogs suppresses

## Risk

- **Surface**: config write path (`io.ts` + `mutate.ts`), warning-only, no behavior change
- **Config files remain valid**: the warning does not block writes, only informs users
- **Comments are still stripped**: this is a warning, not a preservation mechanism
- **$include files covered**: both main config and external include files get warnings

